course: everyday
lesson: 77
title: Hair, nails and ears
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Hair, nails and ears look after themselves in many ways, but they need a little sensible care and a few safety rules.
explain: Long loose hair can catch in moving machines or a flame, so it is tied back near them; and cutting hair does not make it grow back thicker, the cut end only looks blunter.
explain: Dirt and germs collect under nails, so nails are kept short and clean; fingernails are cut following their curve and toenails straight across, so they do not grow into the skin.
explain: Ears clean themselves: wax slowly moves out by itself, so we wash only the outside, and never push cotton buds or anything else inside.
explain: A boy in Vancouver gets water in his ear after swimming; he tilts his head to that side, hops a little, lets it drain and dries the outside with his towel.
fact: Long hair is tied back near machines, fire and in science class, because loose hair can catch in moving parts or a flame.
fact: Cutting hair does not change how it grows; the cut end only looks blunter.
fact: Nails are kept short and clean, and dirt is scrubbed from under them, because germs collect there.
fact: Fingernails are cut following the curve and toenails straight across, with nail clippers or by an adult.
fact: Toenails cut too short or curved can grow into the skin, which is called an ingrown toenail.
fact: Biting nails puts germs in the mouth and hurts the skin around the nails.
fact: A hangnail is clipped with clean clippers, because pulling it tears the skin and can cause infection.
fact: A sore, red, swollen toe beside the nail may be an ingrown toenail, so you tell a parent.
fact: Ears clean themselves, so only the outside is washed, and cotton buds are never pushed inside.
fact: Cotton buds push wax deeper and can hurt the eardrum.
fact: Things like beads and small toys are never put in the ears or nose, and if it happens you tell an adult at once.
fact: Earache can be an infection, so you tell an adult.
fact: Very loud sound for a long time, like music on full volume in earbuds all day, can damage hearing for good.
fact: Water stuck in the ear is drained by tilting the head to that side, because water left there can cause swimmer's ear.
exercise: Why should long hair be tied back in a science lesson with a flame? | Loose hair can catch in the flame | Tied hair helps you think more clearly | The teacher likes tidy hair | Loose hair makes the flame go out
exercise: Does cutting hair make it grow back thicker? | No, the cut end only looks blunter | Yes, every cut doubles the hair that grows back | Yes, but only for children | No, cutting makes it grow thinner
exercise: Why should nails be kept short and clean? | Dirt and germs collect under long nails | Short nails grow much faster than long ones | Long nails make your fingers weak | Clean nails change colour
exercise: How should toenails be cut? | Straight across, with nail clippers | In a deep curve at both of the corners | As short as possible into the skin | With your teeth after a bath
exercise: Why should toenails not be cut too short or curved? | They can grow into the skin | They stop growing for ever | They turn black and fall off at once | They grow back twice as thick
exercise: How can you stop biting your nails? | Keep them short so there is less to bite | Bite only the nails on one hand, never the other | Bite them only when nobody looks | Paint them so the germs cannot see
exercise: You have a little torn bit of skin by your nail, a hangnail. What should you do? | Clip it with clean clippers | Pull it off quickly | Bite it off with your teeth | Leave it and keep picking at it
exercise: Your toe is red, sore and swollen beside the nail. What should you do? | Tell a parent, it may be an ingrown toenail | Dig the nail out yourself with sharp scissors | Squeeze it hard until it stops | Wear tighter shoes to press it down
exercise: How should you clean your ears? | Wash only the outside of the ear | Push cotton buds deep inside | Pour soap into the ear hole | Scrape the wax out with a pencil
exercise: Why should cotton buds not be pushed into the ear? | They push wax deeper and can hurt the eardrum | They make the ear stop producing any wax at all | They are too soft to clean anything | They tickle and make you sneeze
exercise: Your little sister has put a bead up her nose. What should you do? | Tell an adult at once | Push it further in with a finger | Poke it out with a pencil | Wait and see if it falls out next week
exercise: Your ear aches a lot. What should you do? | Tell an adult, it may be an infection | Put a cotton bud deep in it | Pour some cold water into it to cool it | Ignore it until it stops
exercise: Water is stuck in your ear after swimming. What helps? | Tilt your head to that side and let it drain | Push a finger in deep to soak the water up | Leave it there to keep the ear clean | Put more water in to wash it out
exercise: What can water left in the ear after swimming cause? | Swimmer's ear, an ear infection | Better hearing for a day or two | Bigger ears | Nothing at all, ever
test: A girl with long hair is helping her dad with an electric drill. What should she do first? | Tie her hair back | Brush her hair smooth | Let her hair hang over her face | Wear her hair in a loose ribbon
test: A boy in Brisbane cuts his toenails into deep curves at the corners. What could happen? | A toenail could grow into the skin | His toenails would stop growing for good | His toes would get longer | His nails would grow back thicker
test: A friend says you should shave your arms so the hair grows back thick and strong. What is true? | Cutting hair does not change how it grows | Shaving always doubles the hair | Shaving stops hair growing for good | Only arm hair grows back thicker
test: Why do ears not need cleaning inside? | Wax moves out of the ear by itself | Ears never make any wax | Wax is cleaned away from inside by the brain | Ears are cleaned when you sneeze
test: What would probably happen if a child pulled off a hangnail? | The skin could tear and get infected | The nail would grow back faster | The finger would heal quicker | Nothing, it is the best method
test: A boy pushes a cotton bud deep into his ear every day. What is the danger? | He could push wax deeper and hurt his eardrum | His ears would become too clean | His ears would slowly stop hearing music | Nothing, cotton is soft
test: Which habit puts germs into the mouth? | Biting your nails | Keeping your nails short | Scrubbing under your nails | Using nail clippers
test: After a swim in a lake in Ontario a girl's ear feels full of water. What should she do? | Tilt her head and let it drain, then dry the outside | Stick a cotton bud in to soak it up | Shake her head hard while lying in the water | Keep it in so it washes out all the old wax
test: A toddler pushes a pea into his ear. What should his big brother do? | Tell an adult straight away | Try to dig it out with tweezers | Pour water in to float it out | Laugh and wait for it to fall out
test: ear's itchy, gonna dig in with a cotton bud | No, it pushes wax deeper and can hurt the eardrum | Yes, push it right in to clean | Yes, ears need cleaning deep inside every day | Yes, but use a hair clip instead
test: my sis says cutting hair makes it grow back thicker | No, cutting does not change how hair grows | Yes, it grows back thicker each time | Yes, but only if it's cut very short | Yes, it also makes hair grow loads faster
test: lil bro shoved a bead up his nose 😬 | Tell an adult at once | Poke it out with a pencil | Wait and it will come out alone | Tell him to sniff it up hard
test: toe's red n swollen right next to the nail, ouch | It may be an ingrown toenail, tell a parent | Cut the nail very short and curved at the corners | Leave it, it is just a bruise | Squeeze it hard until it pops
explain: A girl in Toronto pushed a cotton bud deep into her ear; it pressed the wax further in and scratched the eardrum, and her ear hurt for days.
explain: A boy in Bristol bit his nails until a fingertip became red, swollen and full of pus, and a doctor had to treat the infection.
fact: Cotton buds pushed into the ear can damage the eardrum and push wax deeper, so doctors say not to put anything in the ear.
fact: Biting nails and picking the skin around them can let germs in and cause painful infections.
test: ear feels blocked, gonna dig with a cotton bud | Don't, it can hurt your eardrum, tell an adult | Push it in as far as it goes | Use a pencil instead, it's thinner and gets right in | Pour cold juice in to loosen it
test: chewed my nail and now my finger is all red n puffy | Show an adult, it may be infected | Chew it more so it heals faster | Hide it in a glove till it goes away on its own | Squeeze it hard to empty it
test: blasting music in earbuds all day on max, fine? | No, loud sound for a long time damages hearing for good | Yes, ears get used to any noise if you give them a few weeks | Yes, earbuds are always safe | Only the left ear gets hurt
test: heard a girl's hair got caught in the drill in tech class and it nearly scalped her, what's the real lesson | Tie long hair back near machines and flames | Long hair should be cut off for every class | Machines only catch short hair, not long | Hold your hair with one hand while drilling
test: my cousin says if u shave ur arm the hair grows back thick and black like a gorilla, true? | No, a myth; cutting hair does not change how it grows | True, every cut hair grows back twice as thick | True, but only on the arms and legs | True, and it grows back in a new colour
test: everyone's saying Ben's got a gross infected finger cos he's a nail-biting freak, should i spread it | No, it's unkind; say nothing, or kindly suggest he tell an adult | Yes, everyone should know he is a freak | Yes, but only to the people at his table | Yes, and take a photo of the finger for the chat
exam: Identify the principal reason for which cotton buds are not to be inserted into the ear. | They push wax deeper and may injure the eardrum | They remove all the wax the ear requires | They are too soft to reach any wax at all | They cause the ears to stop producing wax entirely
exam: Which of the following most accurately characterises the correct manner of cutting toenails? | Straight across, so that they do not grow into the skin | In a deep curve, cut as short as possible | Torn off by hand when they become long | Filed from beneath until they are thin
exam: Select the response consistent with the established facts concerning a hangnail. | It is clipped with clean clippers, since pulling tears the skin | It is pulled off quickly, since this causes less pain and heals sooner | It is bitten off, since saliva heals the skin | It is left to grow until it falls off unaided
exam: Determine the recommended course of action whereas water remains lodged in the ear after swimming. | Tilt the head to that side and allow it to drain | Insert a cotton bud deep into the ear canal | Pour further water in so as to flush it out | Lie on the opposite side so it remains inside
